{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1482","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Playlist"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Arkady has a playlist that initially consists of $$$n$$$ songs, numerated from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ in the order they appear in the playlist. Arkady starts listening to the songs in the playlist one by one, starting from song $$$1$$$. The playlist is cycled, i. e. after listening to the last song, Arkady will continue listening from the beginning."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each song has a genre $$$a_i$$$, which is a positive integer. Let Arkady finish listening to a song with genre $$$y$$$, and the genre of the next-to-last listened song be $$$x$$$. If $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(x, y) = 1$$$, he deletes the last listened song (with genre $$$y$$$) from the playlist. After that he continues listening normally, skipping the deleted songs, and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"forgetting"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" about songs he listened to before. In other words, after he deletes a song, he can't delete the next song immediately."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Here $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor (GCD)"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if the initial songs' genres were $$$[5, 9, 2, 10, 15]$$$, then the playlist is converted as follows: ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 9, 2, 10, 15] $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"9"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 2, 10, 15] $$$\\to$$$ [5, 2, 10, 15] (because $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(5, 9) = 1$$$) $$$\\to$$$ [5, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 10, 15] $$$\\to$$$ [5, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 15] $$$\\to$$$ [5, 2, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"15"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 2, 10, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"15"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"5"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 10, 15] $$$\\to$$$ [5, 10, 15] (because $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(5, 2) = 1$$$) $$$\\to$$$ [5, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 15] $$$\\to$$$ [5, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"15"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] $$$\\to$$$ ... The bold numbers represent the two last played songs. Note that after a song is deleted, Arkady forgets that he listened to that and the previous songs."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given the initial playlist, please determine which songs are eventually deleted and the order these songs are deleted."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10\\,000$$$). Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the number of songs."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the genres of the songs."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single line. First, print a single integer $$$k$$$ — the number of deleted songs. After that print $$$k$$$ distinct integers: deleted songs in the order of their deletion."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n5\n5 9 2 10 15\n6\n1 2 4 2 4 2\n2\n1 2\n1\n1\n1\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2 3 \n2 2 1 \n2 2 1 \n1 1 \n0 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Explanation of the first test case is given in the statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the playlist is converted as follows: ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 2, 4, 2, 4, 2] $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 4, 2, 4, 2] $$$\\to$$$ [1, 4, 2, 4, 2] (because $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(1, 2) = 1$$$) $$$\\to$$$ [1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 2, 4, 2] $$$\\to$$$ [1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 4, 2] $$$\\to$$$ [1, 4, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 2] $$$\\to$$$ [1, 4, 2, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 4, 2, 4, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] $$$\\to$$$ [4, 2, 4, 2] (because $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(2, 1) = 1$$$) $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 2, 4, 2] $$$\\to$$$ ..."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the playlist is converted as follows: ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", 2] $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] $$$\\to$$$ [1] (because $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(1, 2) = 1$$$) $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] $$$\\to$$$ ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"] (Arkady listened to the same song twice in a row) $$$\\to$$$ [] (because $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(1, 1) = 1$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The fourth test case is same as the third after deletion of the second song."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fifth test case, the same song is listened to over and over again, but since $$$\\operatorname{gcd}(2, 2) \\ne 1$$$, it is not deleted."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1482D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1482/problem/D"}